"notes":"Units: millions; teledensity in percent (overall tele-density as published; from Dec 2025 it includes M2M connections). wireless includes 5G FWA. wireless_net_add is TRAI's reported or arithmetically derived (Jan 2026 to Aug 2026 diffs match press-release figures where checked). SERIES BREAK: the Dec 2025 release (PIB) restated Nov 2025 total to 1,297.61m (M2M cellular connections now counted); Jan-Nov 2025 values here are as originally published (ex-M2M), Dec 2025 onward include M2M, so Nov to Dec jump (+71.6m total, 86.77% to 91.74% teledensity) is a definitional change, not growth. Broadband basis also looks restated: Dec 2025 broadband 1,007.35m per PIB, but the Jan 2026 release says prior month was 1,050.60m; Dec value kept as originally released and is not comparable with Jan 2026 onward. Wireline jumps from 38.66m (May 2025) to 47.49m (Jun 2025) as reported by TRAI (apparent reclassification; PR text not checked for reason). Operator data: the TRAI press-release text mainly carries a top-five broadband provider table; operator-wise wireless subscribers (Aug 2026) are from news coverage of TRAI data (TelecomTalk, Tele.net), not directly read from the PDF. Jan-Apr 2025 broadband Jio and Airtel values are Nov 2024 figures carried forward by TRAI because operators did not file in format. Oct 2025 Jio broadband null: extraction returned 908.34 which is clearly erroneous. Jan 2026 Airtel broadband jump (314.26 to 359.29) and BSNL drop (33.03 to 29.64) look like restatement or reclassification and are unverified. Dec 2025 Airtel 314.26 equals Nov 2025 Airtel, possibly an extraction or reporting carry-over; unverified. Wireless tele-density (separate from overall) and MTNL broadband not recorded. Figures were extracted by the WebFetch summarizer, which returned conflicting results on first pass; only values from verbatim-quote passes or cross-checked via arithmetic (wireless + wireline = total) are included. Dec 2025 TRAI PDF has no machine-readable text; Dec figures come from PIB."
